{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"supersonic-shimmery-andeancat","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe completion-verification close gate dies verdict-less when its agentic verify step falls into a tool-call loop: the step budget exhausts, the run surfaces a bare `LLMError` with `diagnostic: null`, and the only documented exit is `--force-close` (an unattested close). Four exhaustions on epic e369; three of four instrumented runs LOOPED, wasting 40-70% of each pathological run (measured on ticket c827-2a23-cd00-473e). Six prior attempts adjusted budgets or added reporting; none acted at the layer where the loop happens.\n\n## Approach\n\nFix the causal chain end to end, in dependency order. First give the repetition detector a signal that separates a k-cycle from healthy breadth (a windowed distinct-ratio produced in `usage_log._repetition_summary` — the existing headline metric is provably inverted on real traces). Independently, replace the provider-broken forced-landing primitive: the `tool_step_limit` empty-filter rewrite in `src/rebar/llm/agent_call.py` causes a Bedrock/Anthropic 400 (`toolConfig` must be defined while history holds `toolUse` blocks — live-proven) — keep tools advertised and steer with synthetic tool results instead. Make bounded recovery reachable for a step-budget exhaustion (`CompletionAgentStep.run` currently catches only `UnretryableOutputError`), and surface the already-computed repetition diagnostic in the `gate_error_v1` sidecar. Then wire the detector to ACT during the run: a typed runaway error classified ahead of the provider-outage fallback in `interpret_failure`, routed into the shipped bounded recovery + tool-free finalizer so the verdict is built from fresh per-criterion evidence, never the poisoned history. Finally, record per-run request/tool-call usage durably by default so the gate can be tuned from data. This fits the problem because every piece wires or repairs a mechanism that already exists and was measured failing — nothing parallel is introduced.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] a runaway tool-call cycle in the completion gate's verify step is detected DURING the run, aborted at that point, and routed to a verdict built from fresh per-criterion evidence — never a bare `LLMError` with `diagnostic: null`; checked by the actuator child's end-to-end test\n- [ ] no code path empties the advertised tool surface mid-run after a tool call has occurred, so the Bedrock/Anthropic toolConfig 400 cannot recur; checked by a regression test asserting tool definitions persist for the whole run\n- [ ] every budget exhaustion or runaway leaves an operator-actionable diagnostic (a `gate_error_v1` sidecar carrying the repetition counters) distinguishing \"it looped\" from \"it ran out of room\"; checked by the diagnostic child's sidecar test\n- [ ] gate runs record request and tool-call usage durably by default, including the loop-vs-breadth axis; checked by the instrumentation child's tests\n- [ ] a healthy high-breadth run is never truncated or aborted by any of the above — budgets remain failure bounds, not workload ceilings; checked by tests replaying the healthy-run profile (0.922 distinct ratio, minimum 24-window ratio 0.833) and asserting no abort\n\n## Child decomposition\n\nChildren by responsibility (dependency order): the detector signal (`distinct_ratio_window`, window 24, trip <= 0.50, single-sourced in `usage_log`) delivers criterion 5's discriminator and is a prerequisite of the actuator and the instrumentation; the protocol-safe forced landing (steering toolset replacing the empty-filter cutoff) delivers criterion 2; recovery reachability (catch extension in `CompletionAgentStep.run`) is a prerequisite of the actuator and the diagnostic surfacing; diagnostic surfacing (sidecar + close-gate message) delivers criterion 3; the actuator (typed runaway error routed to bounded recovery) delivers criterion 1; default-on usage recording delivers criterion 4.","id":"9b71-55b3-1bd1-4a97","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"epic","title":"Completion gate loop breaker: detect runaways during the run, act, and land a verdict"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785954507399157001,"uuid":"b14dd8f8-fd25-41b7-b275-1817117ba126"}